IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `tfm-dates`
IMPORT `tfm-rules`
IMPORT `tfm-seat`

-- Testator's Family Maintenance Act 1912 (Tas) -- worked cases for the claimant's questions (tfm-seat.l4), the date
-- helper (tfm-dates.l4) and the rules (tfm-rules.l4). Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text;
-- none was copied from the encoding's output. Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about
-- the law. The facts are illustrative.
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on material from the Tasmanian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (c) State of Tasmania, CC BY
-- 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`
`any day` MEANS `d` 1 1 2000
`a death in 2025` MEANS `d` 20 6 2025

§§ `the date helper`

#ASSERT `the corresponding day` 3 `months after` (`d` 15 1 2026) EQUALS `d` 15 4 2026
#ASSERT `the corresponding day` 3 `months after` (`d` 30 11 2025) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2026
#ASSERT `the corresponding day` 3 `months after` (`d` 30 11 2023) EQUALS `d` 29 2 2024
#ASSERT `the corresponding day` 3 `months after` (`d` 31 10 2025) EQUALS `d` 31 1 2026
#ASSERT `the corresponding day` 3 `months after` (`d` 31 3 2026) EQUALS `d` 30 6 2026

§§ `ss 2, 3A -- can I apply`

#ASSERT `Can I apply for provision out of the estate` `spouse by marriage` FALSE FALSE `a death in 2025` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "spouse includes" a partner in a significant relationship at the death.
#ASSERT `Can I apply for provision out of the estate` `partner in a significant relationship at the death` FALSE FALSE `a death in 2025` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I apply for provision out of the estate` `child` TRUE FALSE `a death in 2025` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I apply for provision out of the estate` `adopted child` TRUE FALSE `a death in 2025` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I apply for provision out of the estate` `surrogate child` TRUE FALSE `a death in 2025` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A stepchild: the 2015 definition applies to a death on or after its commencement (13 October 2015), s 2(2).
#ASSERT `Can I apply for provision out of the estate` `child of the deceased's spouse` TRUE FALSE (`d` 13 10 2015) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I apply for provision out of the estate` `child of the deceased's spouse` TRUE FALSE (`d` 12 10 2015) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I apply for provision out of the estate` `child whose natural parent was the deceased's spouse when that parent died` TRUE FALSE `a death in 2025` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I apply for provision out of the estate` `child whose natural parent was the deceased's spouse when that parent died` TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2010) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 3A(c): a parent only "if the deceased person dies without leaving a spouse or any children".
#ASSERT `Can I apply for provision out of the estate` `parent` FALSE FALSE `a death in 2025` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I apply for provision out of the estate` `parent` TRUE FALSE `a death in 2025` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 3A(d), (e): a former spouse or partner receiving or entitled to maintenance at the death.
#ASSERT `Can I apply for provision out of the estate` `former spouse, the marriage dissolved or annulled` TRUE TRUE `a death in 2025` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I apply for provision out of the estate` `former spouse, the marriage dissolved or annulled` TRUE FALSE `a death in 2025` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I apply for provision out of the estate` `former partner, the significant relationship ended before the death` FALSE TRUE `a death in 2025` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I apply for provision out of the estate` `former partner, the significant relationship ended before the death` FALSE FALSE `a death in 2025` EQUALS NOTHING
-- A grandchild, sibling or other dependant: s 3A does not name them (fork F3).
#ASSERT `Can I apply for provision out of the estate` `another relationship` FALSE TRUE `a death in 2025` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 3(5) -- the executor applying on my behalf`

#ASSERT `Can the executor apply on my behalf` `child` TRUE FALSE `a death in 2025` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the executor apply on my behalf` `child` TRUE FALSE `a death in 2025` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can the executor apply on my behalf` `parent` TRUE FALSE `a death in 2025` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the executor apply on my behalf` `another relationship` FALSE FALSE `a death in 2025` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 11(1) -- by when`

#ASSERT `By when must I take out my summons` TRUE (`d` 15 1 2026) EQUALS `take out your summons by` (`d` 15 4 2026)
#ASSERT `By when must I take out my summons` TRUE (`d` 30 11 2025) EQUALS `take out your summons by` (`d` 28 2 2026)
#ASSERT `By when must I take out my summons` TRUE (`d` 30 11 2023) EQUALS `take out your summons by` (`d` 29 2 2024)
#ASSERT `By when must I take out my summons` FALSE `any day` EQUALS `the three months have not begun: you may take out your summons now, and at the latest three months after the grant of probate or letters of administration`

§§ `ss 3(4), 11 -- can the Court hear me`

-- Grant 15 January 2026: the last day is 15 April 2026; 16 April is out.
#ASSERT `Can the Court hear my application if I take out the summons on this day` TRUE (`d` 15 1 2026) (`d` 15 4 2026) FALSE FALSE `any day` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Court hear my application if I take out the summons on this day` TRUE (`d` 15 1 2026) (`d` 16 4 2026) FALSE FALSE `any day` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The day of the grant itself, and a day before it ("before ... the date of grant").
#ASSERT `Can the Court hear my application if I take out the summons on this day` TRUE (`d` 15 1 2026) (`d` 15 1 2026) FALSE FALSE `any day` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Court hear my application if I take out the summons on this day` TRUE (`d` 15 1 2026) (`d` 10 1 2026) FALSE FALSE `any day` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No grant yet.
#ASSERT `Can the Court hear my application if I take out the summons on this day` FALSE `any day` (`d` 1 6 2026) FALSE FALSE `any day` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Month ends: grant 30 November 2025, last day 28 February 2026; grant 30 November 2023, last day 29 February 2024.
#ASSERT `Can the Court hear my application if I take out the summons on this day` TRUE (`d` 30 11 2025) (`d` 28 2 2026) FALSE FALSE `any day` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Court hear my application if I take out the summons on this day` TRUE (`d` 30 11 2025) (`d` 1 3 2026) FALSE FALSE `any day` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Court hear my application if I take out the summons on this day` TRUE (`d` 30 11 2023) (`d` 29 2 2024) FALSE FALSE `any day` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Court hear my application if I take out the summons on this day` TRUE (`d` 30 11 2023) (`d` 1 3 2024) FALSE FALSE `any day` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Across the year end: grant 31 October 2025, last day 31 January 2026.
#ASSERT `Can the Court hear my application if I take out the summons on this day` TRUE (`d` 31 10 2025) (`d` 31 1 2026) FALSE FALSE `any day` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Court hear my application if I take out the summons on this day` TRUE (`d` 31 10 2025) (`d` 1 2 2026) FALSE FALSE `any day` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 11(2): time extended to 30 June 2026.
#ASSERT `Can the Court hear my application if I take out the summons on this day` TRUE (`d` 15 1 2026) (`d` 16 4 2026) FALSE TRUE (`d` 30 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Court hear my application if I take out the summons on this day` TRUE (`d` 15 1 2026) (`d` 30 6 2026) FALSE TRUE (`d` 30 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Court hear my application if I take out the summons on this day` TRUE (`d` 15 1 2026) (`d` 1 7 2026) FALSE TRUE (`d` 30 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 3(4): another person's in-time application treated as made by all.
#ASSERT `Can the Court hear my application if I take out the summons on this day` TRUE (`d` 15 1 2026) (`d` 1 9 2026) TRUE FALSE `any day` EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `s 11(2)-(4) -- more time`

#ASSERT `Can I still apply for more time` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I still apply for more time` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 3(1) -- can the Court order provision for me`

#ASSERT `Can the Court order provision for me out of the estate` `child` TRUE FALSE `a death in 2025` TRUE (`d` 15 1 2026) (`d` 1 3 2026) FALSE FALSE `any day` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Adequately provided for: the "if" fails.
#ASSERT `Can the Court order provision for me out of the estate` `child` TRUE FALSE `a death in 2025` TRUE (`d` 15 1 2026) (`d` 1 3 2026) FALSE FALSE `any day` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Out of time with no extension: no jurisdiction.
#ASSERT `Can the Court order provision for me out of the estate` `child` TRUE FALSE `a death in 2025` TRUE (`d` 15 1 2026) (`d` 16 4 2026) FALSE FALSE `any day` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Out of time but extended.
#ASSERT `Can the Court order provision for me out of the estate` `spouse by marriage` FALSE FALSE `a death in 2025` TRUE (`d` 15 1 2026) (`d` 16 4 2026) FALSE TRUE (`d` 30 6 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A parent where the deceased left a child.
#ASSERT `Can the Court order provision for me out of the estate` `parent` TRUE FALSE `a death in 2025` TRUE (`d` 15 1 2026) (`d` 1 3 2026) FALSE FALSE `any day` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not named in s 3A: in time and inadequately provided for, the Act does not answer; out of time, no jurisdiction.
#ASSERT `Can the Court order provision for me out of the estate` `another relationship` FALSE FALSE `a death in 2025` TRUE (`d` 15 1 2026) (`d` 1 3 2026) FALSE FALSE `any day` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can the Court order provision for me out of the estate` `another relationship` FALSE FALSE `a death in 2025` TRUE (`d` 15 1 2026) (`d` 16 4 2026) FALSE FALSE `any day` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A stepchild where the death was before 13 October 2015.
#ASSERT `Can the Court order provision for me out of the estate` `child of the deceased's spouse` TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 6 2015) TRUE (`d` 1 9 2015) (`d` 1 10 2015) FALSE FALSE `any day` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 8(1) -- refusal for character or conduct`

#ASSERT `Can the Court refuse me for my character or conduct` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Court refuse me for my character or conduct` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 7(a) -- the net estate`

#ASSERT `What is the net value of the estate` 500000 50000 20000 30000 EQUALS 400000
#ASSERT `What is the net value of the estate` 100000 60000 40000 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `What is the net value of the estate` 100000 80000 15000 10000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `What is the net value of the estate` 100001 60000 40000 0 EQUALS 1

§§ `s 3(2) -- the form of provision`

#ASSERT `Can my provision take this form` `a lump sum` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my provision take this form` `a life interest or lesser interest in a dwelling-house of the estate` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my provision take this form` `a life interest or lesser interest in a dwelling-house bought for me to live in` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can my provision take this form` `another form` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 9(4) -- remarriage`

#ASSERT `Does my provision continue if I remarry` `spouse by marriage` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does my provision continue if I remarry` `partner in a significant relationship at the death` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does my provision continue if I remarry` `spouse by marriage` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 9(4) speaks only of the spouse.
#ASSERT `Does my provision continue if I remarry` `child` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 9(6) -- notice of an application to change the order`

#ASSERT `Must I be served with notice of an application to change the order` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I be served with notice of an application to change the order` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
